# Packages of the PyTorch environment, envs/torch (roadmap step 4.5): the fork with PyTorch for CUDA 13
# (torch.cuda), to run PyFWI.torchfwi with GPU tensors, exchanged with CuPy through DLPack. PyTorch pins
# its CUDA runtime (13.0, which the driver 580 runs), so the CUDA packages are those it needs, with CuPy
# for CUDA 13 on the same runtime; everything else at the versions of dev.txt:
#   uv pip compile requirements/torch.in \
#       -c <(grep -vE '^(cuda-|cupy-|nvidia-|torch==|triton)' requirements/dev.txt) \
#       --extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu130 --index-strategy unsafe-best-match \
#       --python-version 3.12 -o requirements/torch.txt
numpy
scipy
matplotlib
hdf5storage
requests
segyio
pyopencl
pocl-binary-distribution
cupy-cuda13x[ctk]
cuda-core[cu13]
torch==2.14.1+cu130
pytest
pytest-timeout
coverage
ruff
setuptools
wheel
